WEBVTT

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.470
14 red! 14 red!

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.620
Oh, Madame Martin! I've been waiting for you.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.080
Good evening.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.080
Allow me to join you all.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.330
Take care of this for me.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.420
Sure thing.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.420
Madame, I just knew you would be coming tonight.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.800
A casino without you feels like the dead of winter.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.720
But now springtime has finally arrived.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.680
How was summer in the Bahamas, Jean?

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.640
I'm afraid I had to give that up due to the storms.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.890
Madame, you're beautiful as always.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.520
Oh, Steve! How is your mother faring?

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.950
She has completely recovered.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.910
I didn't think that you'd remember.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.370
Of course I do!

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.200
But thank heavens.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.370
If people close to you fall ill, we won't be able to go on trips together.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.750
Oh, that's true.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.250
Madame, don't be that way!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.960
I was the one who invited you first.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.760
I really wanted to go with you to the Bahamas.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.300
Oh my.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.770
I think you just made me feel a bit disappointed.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.520
Oh, I would never do that...

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.600
I'll certainly think about next time.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.400
Mister.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.690
Would you like to try your luck?

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.070
You try my luck.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.080
Are you sure about this?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.830
Do it.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.500
Don't hold it against me if it doesn't roll right.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.710
Well, let's do it with everyone's least favorite number.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.950
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.080
wondering what I should do right now.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.540
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:18.090
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:23.720
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:29.140
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.600
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:39.900
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:44.200
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:49.290
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.380
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:55.630 --> 00:04:00.970
depend on me for your repairs.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.340
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:11.560
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.860
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:21.900
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:32.040
Expired Fineries

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.880
Care to go another round?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.880
Huh?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.130
Again?

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.720
Now that's just...

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:44.930
It's fine.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.810
Perhaps tonight the unlucky number isn't so unlucky.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.850
What would you like to do, Madame?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:00.110
Let me see how lucky this table is.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.780
Okay.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.850
That roulette wheel seems to favor the number 13.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.310
Everything on the same.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.310
Uh...

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:37.770
Yes, sure thing.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.520
Is he really?

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.520
Yeah right.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.530
Put everything on number 13.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.200
If it's the devil, how's he doing it?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.950
All right, put me in for 6.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.750
Put me down for 25.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.250
10 for 11.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.710
I'll take 9.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.040
All right, let's begin.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.610
That's Mel.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.280
Now she's called "Madame Martin."

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.280
Meeting her will be simple enough.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.750
She's the queen bee at Monte Carlo's number one casino she frequents around midnight.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.960
You can't miss that woman.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.510
She might even stir up your ice-cold blood for all we know.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.640
You said the target is a man.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.180
Mr. Golgo 13...

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:59.140
...care to listen as this poor old man reminisces about days gone past?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.690
Mel was my treasure.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.570
It was eight years ago...

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:12.780
At the time I headed an agricultural co-op.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:22.830
Mel worked at a cheap bar in a small town not far from here cleaning the glasses left behind by the peasants.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.840
During that year, I was all alone, stricken with grief over my wife's death.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:34.510
Then... that man sent me Mel.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:45.860
Despite our age difference, our bodies still connected.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.480
Three months later...

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:55.570
...I polished that precious, unrefined ore with money and lavish places, dressing her up in satins.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:59.000
My Mel was more gorgeous than any jewel.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.000
That woman bedded with me every night.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.000
Those three months were like a dream to me.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:13.010
Then one day, she suddenly vanished from my sight.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:18.010
She also took evidence of my briberies to members of an opposition party.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:23.140
I lost my prestige along with my Mel.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:34.410
Mel has been flitting about with the world's financial bigwigs like a balloon dancing in the wind.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:40.290
Mel's dalliances cause stock prices to go mad, making her a major destabilizing force in the financial world.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:44.370
She moves from one man to the next as
long as they have the wealth and influence.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:49.420
After sucking the nectar dry, she leaves those men, trampling on them like dried out husks.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.890
I still treasure those three months I spent with Mel.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.890
Who I hate is Berne Schultz!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.770
He's a man people call "Chocolate Berne."

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.940
He's the one that's pulling all her strings.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:12.940
Why is a woman like her obeying that man?

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.700
Well...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.620
He...

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:28.670
He was the man who first made a woman out of her.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.840
Anyway...

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:36.880
...this man, Berne Schultz, suddenly disappeared three years ago.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:43.720
He went missing after police organizations began looking for him based on suspicions of espionage.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.190
But he will be in Monte Carlo next week.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:49.730
What makes you say that?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.530
Mel will be seeing the rally races that take place there.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:59.280
Plus, it's such a carefree trip for her that she's only bringing along one maid.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:05.290
His chance to see her after three long years has come.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.920
What's Berne's identifying feature?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.460
He's a small, seedy-looking man.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.300
He's probably as tall as me.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.800
However, now that he's internationally wanted...

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.470
...he might have transformed his face, being the man he is.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:27.390
There's another feature a scalpel can't touch - his character.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.980
The term "fungal parasite" would describe him perfectly.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.730
He's always following her around.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.490
He never-

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.320
Gambling is learning when to quit while ahead, Mister.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.370
I just robbed that man of his good luck.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.240
Who is he?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.450
Oh yes...

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:33.670
He told me he's here for next week's rally race when we met at the bar.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.170
He's a racer?

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.000
Well, no...

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.340
I believe he did say his name was Mr. Togo.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.220
Yes.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.890
Excuse me for a moment.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.360
Pardon my absence.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.490
It's from Madame Martin.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.790
It's her apology for ruining your luck.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.380
That's a treat from Madame Martin. Won't you accept?

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.430
I don't make that a habit.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.890
You can still be appreciative without saying that...

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:31.730
Madame, you're leaving already?

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.020
I'm feeling rather unpleasant this evening.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.520
If I may...

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:40.400
Mel, don't loiter around, go and hail a taxi.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:40.780
Yes ma'am!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:41.900
Mel?

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.570
Madame Martin.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.660
If you need a car, let me drive you.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.580
Pierre, it's been a while!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.790
When did you arrive in Monte Carlo?

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.090
The day before.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:07.430
Where did that Mel go?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.220
It's fine.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.770
She'll just get home by taxi anyway.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.730
Here, we hope you'll come again!

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.320
Say, who was that man?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.690
Hmm, I'm afraid I don't know.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:28.910
Ever since Count Martin passed away, she's been courted by countless men.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.960
Anyways, I wish you best of luck, Mister.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.090
Oh, Madame!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.300
What are you doing?

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.920
Did you find a taxi?

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:48.800
Harlots like you aren't welcome here!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.390
You're wrong!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.850
I was just asking her for directions!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:57.020
Madame, let's leave it as it is and go.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:59.900
We're sorry. Here take this.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.060
Where are we headed?

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.100
To my late husband's mountain villa.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.980
It's a bit far, though.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:45.530
Extending my time with you will be pure bliss.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.570
My, what a silver tongue.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.380
<i>No car.</i>

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:56.310
<i>He probably left after dropping her off.</i>

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.680
<i>Bodyguards?</i>

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.110
<i>A woman.</i>

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.570
<i>Mel?</i>

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.740
<i>Or Madame?</i>

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.420
Rock?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:53.380
Carson?

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.760
Those two won't be answering.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.140
You're the one who sent those hired guns to kill me, right?

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.310
Is the man inside Chocolate Berne?

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.100
Hmph.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.770
Your client is supposed to be dead.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.320
Why are you still on the job?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.570
I accepted my assignment while my client was still alive.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:22.330
Is that man inside Chocolate Berne?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:23.080
Hmph!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.780
We've brought the vehicle you ordered.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.490
Very good.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:04.790
Have a nice outing.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.200
Thank you.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.090
<i>So that's what it was.</i>

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:03.070
Turning the Loews Hairpin, it's Sebastian Auriol in the lead!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.240
Imon Mäkinen is in close second!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:17.330
Ooh! At the Nouvelle Chicane, Imon Mäkinen crashed into the guardrail! Is he all right?

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:31.720
It looks like Mäkinen and the navigator Kankkunen is all right.

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:33.770
Thank goodness for that!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:39.110
But now, turning the last corner, Sebastian Auriol is coming down the stretch!

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:09.430
Chocolate!

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:10.680
Chocolate!!

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.930
Don't leave me!

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:14.600
Don't leave me alone!

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.430
No! Chocolate!

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:18.940
<i>A fungal parasite, huh?</i>

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:23.980
My...

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:26.700
My Chocolate Berne!

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.570
No!!

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.960
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:53.180
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:59.270
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:04.110
of flowers.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:11.740
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:16.330
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:19.710
I had a dream.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:25.420
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:32.010
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.560
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.060
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.650
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.820
I won't.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.380
Christmas Eve - 10:00.

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:07.750
Golgo entered a hotel to do a shooting.

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:13.840
12:00 - Golgo encountered the hotel's
female special investigator named Dahl.

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:16.810
Christmas - 9:30.

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:20.520
Golgo faced his target aiming his M16...

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:25.360
Next time on Golgo 13: Christmas 24 Hours.

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:27.270
Christmas 24 Hours

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:29.360
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
